  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **I Could Never Take The Place Of Your Man** (1 review): Reviewer liked the Prince cover, played alongside Infancy, Steam Engine, and Run Thru [4]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Raspberry Beret**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- **Young Americans**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- **I Could Never Take The Place Of Your Man**: back after 67 archived shows (1363 days); rare: 8 archived performances [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **mmj2016-05-13.mk21.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 23 songs; 147 min; rated 2.5/5 by 2 [1]\n- **mmj2016-05-13.mk4**: source not stated; 22 songs; 143 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Reviewer was twenty and discovered the band at Forecastle 2015, hearing friends howling [3]\n- This night was better than the first, which included Off The Record and Lay Low [4]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **mmj2016-05-13.mk21.flac16**: taped by Brian Porter; source: Schoeps mk21 (FOB/ORTF wide) > kcy > Sonosax SX-M2/LS2 > Sony M10 (24/48) [1]\n- **mmj2016-05-13.mk4**: taped by Brent Stober; transferred by Brent Stober; source: Schoeps mk4 (DIN) > kc5 >cmc6xt > Sonosax sx-m2 > Sound Device 702 @ 24/48 [2]. Also: Uploader notes the file contains tracks one, nine, seventeen, and twenty-two [2]",
